    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.add_caveman_graph - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.add_caveman_graph.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_caveman_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: \"Add a caveman graph: separate cliques of equal size.\"\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_caveman_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: \"Add a caveman graph: separate cliques of equal size.\"\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.add_caveman_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: \"Add a caveman graph: separate cliques of equal size.\"\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nAdd a caveman graph: separate cliques of equal size.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L16189-L16330){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.add_caveman_graph(\n    num_cliques,\n    clique_size,\n    community_attr=\"community\",\n    type=None,\n    label=True,\n    rel=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Caveman graph](../assets/graphs/add-caveman-graph.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three caveman graphs side by side, each clique in its own color: two triangles, three triangles, and three complete graphs on four nodes. The cliques are completely separate, with no edges between them, so each one is its own community.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nCreates `num_cliques` complete graphs (\"caves\") of `clique_size` nodes each and leaves\nthem unconnected. With `L` cliques of `k` nodes, the graph has `L * k` nodes,\n`L * k(k - 1)/2` edges, and `L` connected components. It is the extreme case of community\nstructure, with every edge inside a community and none between them, and the starting\npoint for the connected and relaxed caveman graphs (see `add_connected_caveman_graph()`\nand `add_relaxed_caveman_graph()`).\n\nEach node's cave (`0`, `1`, ...) is stored in the `community_attr=` node attribute, so\nthe planted communities can be compared with what a detection method finds. The caves\nare created one after another, each as a consecutive run of node IDs; in a directed\ngraph every edge points from the earlier-created node to the later one. The graph is\nappended without touching or connecting to existing nodes, and the whole construction\nis recorded as a single step.\n\nCaveman graphs are useful for:\n\n- sanity checks for community detection, which should recover the caves exactly\n- modeling isolated, tightly knit groups (Watts's \"caveman world\" of small societies)\n- a baseline against which to compare the relaxed and connected variants\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[num_cliques]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of cliques. Must be at least `1`.\n\n<code>[clique_size]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of nodes in each clique. Must be at least `1`.\n\n<code>[community_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;community&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute that records each node's clique index. Default is\n    `\"community\"`. Pass `None` to skip storing it.\n\n<code>[type]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `type` attribute of every new node. If `None` (default),\n    no `type` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[label]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), each new node is labelled with its node ID as a string; a label\n    that is already used raises `ValueError` before anything is added. If `False`, the\n    nodes are left unlabelled.\n\n<code>[rel]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `rel` attribute of every new edge. If `None` (default),\n    no `rel` attribute is set.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Self for method chaining. The graph is modified in place.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `num_cliques=` or `clique_size=` is less than `1`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~add_connected_caveman_graph`) \n\n:   Join the caves in a ring by rewiring one edge in each.\n\n[](`~add_relaxed_caveman_graph`) \n\n:   Rewire cave edges at random with a given probability.\n\n[](`~add_ring_of_cliques`) \n\n:   Join complete graphs in a ring with one added edge each.\n\n[](`~modularity`) \n\n:   Score a partition such as the planted caves.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA caveman graph is a set of separate complete graphs, the caves. Three caves of four\nnodes give `12` nodes, `3 * 6 = 18` edges and three separate components:\n\n::: {#75d77217 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_caveman_graph(num_cliques=3, clique_size=4)\n\n(\n    graph.count_nodes(),\n    graph.count_edges(),\n    graph.count_weakly_connected_components(),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(12, 18, 3)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe `community` attribute holds the cave of each node. Since no edge leaves a cave, this\npartition reaches `1 - 1/3`, the highest modularity any split into three groups can\nscore:\n\n::: {#eefd82bf .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph.modularity(\"community\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n0.6666666666666666\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Separate caves or a ring of them\n\nThe caves on the left, each node colored by its cave. `add_connected_caveman_graph()`, on\nthe right, moves one edge end in each cave to the next cave, which joins the caves in a\nring with the same number of edges:\n\n::: {#2b073921 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nconnected = ec.Graph().add_connected_caveman_graph(\n    num_cliques=3, clique_size=4\n)\n\nconnected.count_edges(), connected.is_connected()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(18, True)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {layout-ncol=\"2\"}\n\n::: {#93a072a1 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph.plot(\n    color_by=\"community\", label_by=\"label\",\n    width=320, height=320, legend=False, seed=1,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"320\" height=\"320\" viewBox=\"6.1 16.1 307.7 307.7\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"6.1\" y=\"16.1\" width=\"307.7\" height=\"307.7\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<line x1=\"68.7\" y1=\"85.8\" x2=\"65.1\" y2=\"122.4\" stroke=\"#e15759\" stroke-width=\"2.2800000000000002\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" strok